  "notes": "USAGE:\n{棄権|きけん} literally means \"abandoning a right\" ({棄|き} = discard, {権|けん} = right). It is used both in political contexts (not voting) and sports contexts (withdrawing from competition).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {棄権|きけん}する: to abstain / to withdraw\n- {棄権|きけん}{率|りつ}: abstention rate\n- {途中|とちゅう}{棄権|きけん}: mid-event withdrawal\n- {棄権|きけん}{票|ひょう}: abstention vote\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{辞退|じたい} is declining an offer or nomination before participating, while {棄権|きけん} is giving up a right or withdrawing after entry.",
